2026-06-14 15:29:36.166 INFO  - OUTPUT {"coverage_rating":1,"coverage_justification":"Data Backups is architecturally relevant to device restart/shutdown recovery but does not prevent or contain the technique itself. The control addresses post-incident recovery by enabling restoration of configurations and control logic after a device has been forcibly restarted or shut down, thus reducing recovery time and operational downtime. However, it provides no reliable prevention of the restart/shutdown action occurring in the first place. The technique's impact—unexpected device restart/shutdown causing disruption to critical physical processes—still occurs regardless of backup availability. While backups reduce the blast radius by enabling faster restoration, they do not mitigate the immediate operational disruption during the restart/shutdown event, which may occur at critical moments when rapid response is needed. Backups also do not address the root cause (unauthorized access to device control interfaces or network protocols). In a scenario where an attacker initiates a device restart during a time-sensitive process, the backup cannot prevent the process interruption or physical consequences that may result from sudden shutdown. The control is only useful after the attack has already succeeded in disrupting operations."}
